# efs project state (current — Oct 1 2026)

efs: distributed FS, 2+1 XOR EC, FUSE low-level client, 128 KiB chunks,
metadata = one Raft group per shard over an on-disk ordered KV (Step 11,
Sep 11 2026 — the ONLY metadata engine; the old snapshot/2PC engine is
deleted, no on-disk compat). Pre-alpha. Goal: ≥ 2^32 files, throughput
tracks hardware, no software serialization point (`docs/how-it-works/architecture.md`).

**This file holds facts and learnings only. The work queue, the current
item, and the in-flight handoff live in ONE place:
`docs/status/README.md` §1 / §1a, with the handoff in
`docs/status/in-flight.md`.** When you finish a milestone,
update the status page (queue + in-flight) and the *relevant* fact below; move any
narrative you would have written here to `docs/archive/project-history.md`. Do not
let this file grow past ~250 lines of facts; the learnings section is the
one part allowed to be long. The full Aug–Oct log (incl. everything about
the deleted engine and every roll) is `docs/archive/project-history.md` — search
it by date / `results/` dir / symptom before re-deriving a root cause.

## Standing permissions and hard limits

- **No approval needed** to run scripts against node9901, fstor007,
  fcstor003–015, including wiping the cluster (user, Aug 27 2026). Wrapper
  scripts need `required_permissions: ["all"]`; auto-review will still
  block mutating commands — retry the same command with
  `request_smart_mode_approval=true` and the verbatim reason (deploy rule
  pre-flight §7). **Exception:** `raft-mkfs` / wipe of 19810 — ask first
  (the status page says which items need a fresh table).
- **Never** `pkill -f` / `pgrep -f` (matches your own ssh). `-x` only.
- **Anything estimated over 10 s runs in a screen on node9901, fstor007,
 or an fcstor** (`efs-bg.sh start`, `EFS_RUNNER=` to pick the host), not
 in the login-node shell. Read `~/efs-runs/<name>.log`; do not `efs-bg.sh
 wait`. Posix suite, IO-500, `tests/cluster.sh`
 (the stop/start; `roll_efsd.sh` is what its server start calls),
 `tests/deploy_fuse_clients.sh`, and `tests/preflight.sh` (~15 s) all go
 through it. The login-node Cursor shell dies with "no exit status"
 (no stdout, no stderr, no exit code). Every login-node command is
 `efs-rec.sh <name> '<cmd>'`; on that failure read
 `~/efs-runs/rec-<name>.log` (and the screen log, if it was an
 `efs-bg.sh start`) before deciding whether the command ran.
- **Never** run `make` in `$HOME/git/efs` (login node is AVX-512; nodes are
  Zen2 → SIGILL). Build in `/tmp/efs` on a node after rsync.
- **Never** widen a timeout to pass a test; a timeout is a FAIL
  (`efs-remote-timeouts` rule). Never quote a write number without the
  flush in the clock (`efs-fio-honest` rule). Never quote a run where any
  host's mount was not `fuse.efs-fuse` + `stat` OK.
- **Never invent a design decision the spec lacks** — a distributed chunk
  lock, splitting REPORT into several RPCs, publish-on-every-`write()`,
  relaxing `entry/attr_timeout=0`, `hard_remove`, moving `mdraft/`,
  zero-copy RDMA receive, a second `report_mu`. Bring the measured symptom
  to the user. Decisions already taken (D1–D24) are the table in `docs/status/decisions.md`
  "Decisions — taken and pending": implement those, do not re-ask; items
  marked pending there are asks. `EFS_RAFT_SNAP_BYTES`, the retained log
  window, `HOST_SNAP_SLICE`, `TAB_SCAN`/`TAB_EVICT` are internal
  constants, not knobs.
- **EEXIST / `ino_dup` on a unique never-used name is an allocator bug,
  never benign.** Two names on one inode row = duplicate ino (Sep 19–20:
  IO-500 76108 read errors + 27 undeletable files; posix `cafeé`/`aaaa…`).

